+# Back-office readiness: known problems
+
+Problems found in the code as it stands, in the areas the back office will rely on: draft orders,
+stock allocation, fulfillment, returns/refunds, the Transactions API, background tasks and webhooks.
+This document lists problems only. It does not propose fixes.
+
+Audit date: 2026-11-24, at commit `b8025bac2a`.
+
+## How to read this
+
+Each entry says what goes wrong, when, and where in the code. Paths are relative to the repo root.
+
+**Status** tells you how far each entry was checked:
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| Reproduced | The code shape was run in a minimal script (Django 5.2.19, the pinned version) and misbehaved as described. |
+| Verified | The cited lines were re-read and do what the entry says. For races this means the missing lock or re-check is confirmed; the race itself was not run. |
+| Traced | Found by a code-tracing pass; the cited lines were not independently re-read. |
+| Plausible | The code was read, but the failure needs timing or configuration that was not reproduced. |
+
+**When** tells you how likely you are to hit it:
+
+- *Every time*: deterministic for the described input.
+- *Concurrent*: needs two requests for the same object at nearly the same moment. That means two
+  employees, a double click, a client retry, or a staff action racing a payment-app callback or a
+  background task.
+- *Setting-dependent*: only with a non-default setting, which is named.
+
+### Limits of this audit
+
+- Nothing was run against a database and the Saleor test suite was not run. Everything except the
+  entries marked "Reproduced" comes from reading code.
+- The dashboard front end is not in this repository. Where an entry needs an unusual API input
+  (a negative quantity, a line from another order), whether the dashboard can send it is unknown.
+  Any app or script using the API can.
+- The lines checked with `git blame` date from long-standing commits, so these are not recent local
+  regressions.
+
+## Read these first
+
+The problems most likely to cost money, stock accuracy or staff time.
+
