+## Fulfillment
+
+<a id="fu-1"></a>
+### FU-1. Two partial fulfillments of the same line at once ship more than was ordered
+
+- **What happens:** `create_fulfillments` locks and re-reads the order lines, but uses the fresh rows
+  only for validation. The fulfilled quantity is then written from the copies loaded before the
+  lock: `line.quantity_fulfilled += quantity` followed by a bulk update. Line of 4, two employees
+  each fulfil 2: both fulfillments are created and stock drops by 4, but the line records 2
+  fulfilled. The order shows 2 still to ship, and a third fulfillment is accepted.
+- **When:** concurrent. A second request that exceeds the remainder is caught; partial ones are not.
+- **Where:** `saleor/order/actions.py:1066-1073`, `1209-1218`, `1292-1300`;
+  `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/order_fulfill.py:218-245`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+<a id="fu-2"></a>
+### FU-2. Approving a fulfillment twice decreases stock twice and issues gift cards twice
+
+- **What happens:** the "waiting for approval" check runs once, on a copy read before the
+  transaction. `approve_fulfillment` takes no lock and sets the status unconditionally. A second
+  approval waits for the first and then runs the whole body again: stock is decreased again, a
+  second set of gift cards with new codes is created and emailed, and events, webhooks and the
+  customer email are duplicated.
+- **When:** concurrent.
+- **Where:** `saleor/order/actions.py:864-942`;
+  `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/fulfillment_approve.py:55`, `86-106`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+<a id="fu-3"></a>
+### FU-3. Cancelling a fulfillment twice restocks twice; approve racing cancel leaves contradictory state
+
+- **What happens:** `cancel_fulfillment` locks the fulfillment row but never looks at its status
+  again.
+  - Two cancels: stock and the allocation are increased twice and `quantity_fulfilled` is reduced
+    twice. It can go negative, since nothing in the database prevents it.
+  - Approve commits first, then cancel: the cancel takes the "was waiting" branch and returns no
+    stock, although the approval removed it.
+  - Cancel commits first, then approve: the cancelled fulfillment is set back to fulfilled and
+    stock is decreased, while `quantity_fulfilled` stays reduced, so the units can be fulfilled again.
+- **When:** concurrent.
+- **Where:** `saleor/order/actions.py:808-861`; `saleor/order/utils.py:662-674`;
+  `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/fulfillment_cancel.py:52-127`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+### FU-4. Orders in any status can be fulfilled, and cancel races fulfil
+
+- **What happens:** `orderFulfill` checks payment, duplicates, quantities and preorder, but not the
+  order's status. Draft, unconfirmed, cancelled and expired orders can be fulfilled through the API.
+  The order status is then recomputed from quantities alone, so a cancelled order becomes fulfilled.
+  `orderCancel` checks `can_cancel()` before its transaction and writes the status without locking
+  the order, so a cancel and a fulfil at the same moment both succeed: the customer gets both emails.
+  An unconfirmed order that is fulfilled can no longer be confirmed, so the confirmation webhook,
+  email and gift-card charge never run.
+- **When:** every time through the API for the status gap; concurrent for the cancel race.
+- **Where:** `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/order_fulfill.py:190-203`;
+  `saleor/order/utils.py:159-207`; `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/order_cancel.py:21-66`;
+  `saleor/order/actions.py:422-454`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+### FU-5. A fulfil request accepts lines from a different order
+
+- **What happens:** the order lines are loaded by id with no check that they belong to the order
+  named in the request. The fulfillment is attached to order X while its lines, quantities and stock
+  changes belong to order Y. Y's status is not updated. A channel-restricted employee can fulfil
+  lines of an order in a channel they cannot access, and an unpaid order can be fulfilled through a
+  paid one.
+- **When:** every time such a request is sent.
+- **Where:** `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/order_fulfill.py:216-223`;
+  `saleor/order/actions.py:1294-1305`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+### FU-6. Refund and return fulfillments can be "cancelled"
+
+- **What happens:** the only guard is `status != CANCELED`. Cancelling a refunded, returned or
+  replaced fulfillment with a warehouse restocks its lines and reduces `quantity_fulfilled`. The
+  refund record becomes cancelled, the refunded lines look fulfillable again, and for a refund of
+  never-shipped items the restock adds inventory that never left the warehouse.
+- **When:** every time through the API.
+- **Where:** `saleor/order/models.py:845-846`;
+  `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/fulfillment_cancel.py:52-75`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+### FU-7. Two fulfillments of one order can get the same number
+
+- **What happens:** the fulfillment number is "current maximum plus one", read without a lock, and
+  there is no unique constraint. Two fulfillments created together both become, say, `1234-2`.
+  History entries identify fulfillments only by that number.
+- **When:** concurrent.
+- **Where:** `saleor/order/models.py:832-843`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
+
+### FU-8. No fulfillment can be cancelled on an order that contains a gift card
+
+- **What happens:** the cancel mutation rejects any order with a gift-card line, before looking at
+  which fulfillment is being cancelled. A fulfillment of physical items created with the wrong
+  warehouse or quantity cannot be undone, and the order cannot be cancelled while it exists. The
+  message is "Cannot cancel fulfillment with gift card lines." even when the fulfillment has none.
+- **When:** every time.
+- **Where:** `saleor/graphql/order/mutations/fulfillment_cancel.py:77-100`.
+- **Status:** Verified.
